  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): オシロイバナ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%82%B7%E3%83%AD%E3%82%A4%E3%83%90%E3%83%8A",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 106352008,
      "text": "オシロイバナ は、オシロイバナ科の多年草。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Mirabilis jalapa",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirabilis_jalapa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1376309656,
      "text": "Mirabilis jalapa, the marvel of Peru or four o'clock flower, is the most commonly grown ornamental species of Mirabilis plant, and is available in a range of colors. Mirabilis in Latin means wonderful and Jalapa is the state capital of Veracruz in Mexico. Mirabilis jalapa is believed to have been cultivated by the Aztecs for medicinal and ornamental purposes."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Mirabilis jalapa",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirabilis_jalapa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 175700782,
      "text": "Mirabilis jalapa, llamada comúnmente dondiego de noche, dompedros, periquito, maravilla del Perú, clavellina o nochera, es una especie de planta herbácea del género Mirabilis de la familia Nyctaginaceae; es la más cultivada, como planta ornamental, del género. Oriunda de México a Argentina."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Mirabilis jalapa",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirabilis_jalapa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 239601191,
      "text": "Mirabilis jalapa, la Belle-de-nuit ou Merveille du Pérou, est une espèce de plantes herbacées vivaces de la famille des Nyctaginacées, poussant aussi bien dans les jardins que dans les milieux incultes. Originaire d'Amérique subtropicale, elle fut introduite en Europe à la fin du XVIe siècle. Elle tient son nom de sa principale caractéristique, ses fleurs s'ouvrent pleinement la nuit et se referment au petit matin. La plante très facile de culture fournit de juillet à novembre une profusion ininterrompue de graines noires et on la trouve souvent se replantant d'elle-même à l'état sauvage. Ses couleurs qui sont le rose, le rouge, le jaune, le blanc et le mauve peuvent être mélangées au sein d'une même fleur."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Maravilha (planta)",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maravilha_(planta)",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 71418509,
      "text": "Maravilha é uma planta ornamental que disponibiliza a variedade de cores como a cor vermelha, rosa, amarela, branca, etc. Em seu nome, Mirabilis, do latim, significa maravilha ou admirável, e Jalapa é um nome de uma cidade mexicana, mas dizem que essa planta tem sido exportada a partir dos Andes Peruanos, em 1540."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Bunga pukul empat",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunga_pukul_empat",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29220729,
      "text": "Bunga pukul empat atau Mirabilis Jalapa merupakan spesies tanaman hias yang paling umum ditanam dari genus Mirabilis dan tersedia dalam berbagai warna. Mirabilis dalam Bahasa Latin berarti indah dan Jalapa yang merupakan nama ibu kota negara bagian Veracruz di Meksiko. Tanaman ini dibudidayakan oleh suku Aztec sebagai tanaman obat maupun tanaman hias."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Mirabilis jalapa § Cultivation",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirabilis_jalapa#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1376309656,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "The plant does best in full sun. Often in the sun the leaves wither, then return vigorously in the evening, when temperatures start to fall and the sun sets. It cannot stand the cold as the aerial part, with the first frosts, deteriorates and can die, but the underground part that can return to vegetate in spring remains vital. The plant will self-seed, often spreading rapidly if left unchecked in a garden. Some gardeners recommend that the seeds should be soaked before planting, but this is not totally necessary. In North America, the plant perennializes in warm, coastal environments, particularly in USDA zones 7–10. The plant is easy to grow, as long as it is sunny or partially shaded. Under these conditions, it grows very quickly.\nIt grows preferably in light soil, rich in humus and well draining, it is neutral side acidity (pH). Pot cultivation is always possible with a mixture of 80% soil and 20% garden soil and a very deep container with the tubers being put at a depth of 10 cm. It is usually sown from mid-February to May. The seeds germinate rapidly at a temperature of 18 °C.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
